    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d906">

                <pb facs="0813" n="801" xml:id="pg801"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.248/731: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ankara</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-09-24T19:00:00+03:00">September 24,
                            1942—7 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 25—2:05 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>951. In course of a lengthy conversation yesterday with Prime Minister<anchor
                        n="98" xml:id="d906-f1"/> I brought matters enumerated below to his
                    attention and received following replies.</p>
                <p>1. Secret instruments which are part of equipment of United States Army bombers
                    interned in Turkey.</p>
                <p>Saraçoğlu gave peremptory instructions in my presence that interned aviators be
                    given access to instruments for purpose of delivering them to Embassy. Seals are
                    to be broken in presence of aviators and coding machines and codes are to be
                    delivered to Embassy. $15,000 of United States currency carried by planes is
                    likewise to be delivered to Embassy.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d906-f1" n="98" xml:id="d906-f1-content">
                <p>Sükrü Saraçoğlu, former Minister for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
